  "title": "Calibrated Forecast Pool \u2014 sealed probabilities and conserved Brier payouts",
  "notes": "Forecasters seal identity/question/contract-bound probabilities and equal synthetic stakes, then reveal. Validators independently fetch frozen sources and interpret a binary criterion; integer Brier scores deterministically split the pot, with dust ordering, unrevealed-stake forfeiture and one-shot withdrawals. Permissionless deadline expiry refunds unresolved pools. Two source-matched StudioNet demos: CPython distutils removal resolved YES and paid 172/128/0 from 300 units; expiry refunded both revealed and unrevealed 100-unit stakes. All 24 transactions finalized: 20 successes, 4 expected rollbacks; zero units held. 85 direct tests and lint/SDK validation pass. Local comparisons disclose shared commit-reveal and evidence-resolution plumbing; the distinction is sealed-probability scoring with conserved allocation. Limits: synthetic ledger, no native/token custody; normalized pooled payouts do not guarantee truthful-reporting incentives.",
